<</Type/StructElem/S/H2/P 1575 0 R/T(III. THE RENEWED PROSECUTION OF MR. SMOLLETT WAS INVALID ON ITS FACE BECAUSE (1) STATUTORY AUTHORITY WAS LACKING FOR THE APPOINTMENT OF A SPECIAL PROSECUTOR, (2) THE APPOINTMENT ORDER WAS VAGUE AND OVERBROAD, (3) THE APPOINTMENT OF A PRIVATE SPECIAL PROSECUTOR, I.E., DAN WEBB AND THE OFFICE OF THE SPECIAL PROSECUTOR, WAS NOT STATUTORILY ALLOWED WHERE PUBLIC AGENCIES WERE WILLING AND ABLE TO ACCEPT THE APPOINTMENT, AND (4) THE CIRCUIT COURT JUDGE IMPROPERLY DENIED THE DEFENSE MOTION FOR SUBSTITUTION OF JUDGE FOR CAUSE BASED ON HIS EXPRESS BIAS AND PREJUDGMENT OF GUILT TOWARDS MR. SMOLLETT, RENDERING EVERY SUBSEQUENT RULING AND ACTION IN THIS CASE NULL AND VOID.)/K[911 0 R]>>
endobj
